# Railway deployment configuration
# This file helps Railway understand how to build and run your application

# Build command (optional - Railway auto-detects Python)
# build: pip install -r requirements.txt

# Start command (defined in Procfile)
# start: streamlit run app.py --server.port=$PORT --server.enableCORS=false

# Environment variables needed:
# OPENAI_API_KEY=your_openai_api_key_here

# Railway will automatically:
# 1. Detect this is a Python application
# 2. Install dependencies from requirements.txt
# 3. Use the Procfile to start the application
# 4. Set PORT environment variable
# 5. Expose the application on a public URL